A||||10||skitime||Speedometer reads too fast on 88 GT||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||11-11-2000||09:34 PM||||Our 88 GT has stock tires sizes front and rear (210/60/15 & 205/60/15) but the speedometer read about seven miles an hour too fast.  Does anyone else have this problem and what do you do about it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||11-11-2000||09:48 PM||||Possibly a typo, but 210/60/15 isn't stock rear tire size.||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||11-11-2000||09:52 PM||||You are right, I checked and it is 215/60/15. Thanks for the correction||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-11-2000||09:56 PM||||Speedos are not known for being entirely accurate. The speedo readings are taken from the tranny(rear wheel speed). Possibly false from factory, or maybe what you used to measure is off.<P>I have a spec sheet around here, that tells what Fiero speedo displays at certain speeds, and what the real speed is. Will have to dig it out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||11-11-2000||10:00 PM||||Another question related to this problem, if the speedometer is off aproximately 10% would that mean the odometer is also off 10% and would my car have 10% less miles on it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||11-11-2000||10:03 PM||||okay I am an idiot but the speedometer actually read too slow now that I am thinking about it.  At 67 miles an hour the speedometer read 60.  Sorry for the confusion.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fldevel||11-11-2000||10:14 PM||||stupid question ? how do you know you where doing 67 if your speedy meeter sed 60 ?? <BR>usualy if you go by the next telephone pole before you can say fiero .. you going too fast||||reg||1
Z||000007||skitime||11-11-2000||10:23 PM||||Beside passing everything in site when going the speed limit according to the speedometer, we drove with another car with two way radios to verify the discrepency. The Pontiac Grand Prix has a digital speedometer which has been verified by State Troopers and speeding tickets (mine). The trooper have always been right.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||11-11-2000||10:47 PM||||Funny you should mention that, I was just looking through some of my old magazines and in the March 88 Motor Trend they noticed it was 3 mph too much, in a brand spankin' new GT....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||robertjay||11-12-2000||01:44 AM||||I installed 225/50R 16 tires on mine and now with a radar, mine is dead nuts accurate.  Which would lead me to beleive it was reading too fast to begin with, but I never checked.||||reg||1
Z||000010||pHoOl||11-12-2000||02:29 PM||||I always try to check mine when the police have those little carts on the side of the road that read off your speed, and it seems that mine is pretty close to accurate, but i'll check it again next time i see it.  Fiero56, email me that chart if you find it<P>janikm@river.it.gvsu.edu<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
